Open a new Terminal in (VS Code IDE) and run the following commands:
node -v
npm -v
-------------------------------
Create a new directory called “DemoApp” for your project and navigate into it via Terminal:
Create a sub directory called “server”:
mkdir server
cd server
-------------------------------------------
Initialize a new Node.js project:
npm init -y
npm install express cors dotenv mongoose nodemon
--------------------------------------------
Next, create a new JavaScript file named "server.js" under server directory.
-------------------------------------------------
Open package.json and modify the “scripts” and “main” as given below:-
-------------------------------------------------------------------
{
  "name": "server",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "nodemon server.js"
  },
  "keywords": [],
  "author": "",
  "license": "ISC",
  "type": "commonjs",
  "dependencies": {
    "cors": "^2.8.6",
    "dotenv": "^17.3.1",
    "express": "^5.2.1",
    "mongoose": "^9.3.3",
    "nodemon": "^3.1.14"
  }
}
-------------------------------------------
Finally, Save all and Run Server Application
npm run dev
